<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>CQA - Public Transparency Portal</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:wght@600;700;800&family=Inter:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    <script src="/js/offline-db.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/connection-prompt.js"></script>

    <meta name="theme-color" content="#251d3a">
    <!-- Fullscreen on first tap (phones only) — it cannot run on page load,
         requestFullscreen() needs a user gesture. See the file for details. -->
    <script src="/js/mobile-fullscreen.js" defer></script>
    <!-- Animation stack: GSAP + ScrollTrigger for scroll-driven reveals/parallax (native scroll, no smooth-scroll library) -->
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.12.5/dist/gsap.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.12.5/dist/ScrollTrigger.min.js"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/offline-pill.css">

    <style>
        /* The "you're viewing offline" chip and its red server-unavailable twin
           are /css/offline-pill.css now — the same floating chip the survey and
           the office portal use, fixed and centred just below the header rather
           than scrolling away with the page. syncHeaderSpacer() feeds it this
           page's measured header height (see --offline-pill-top below).
           .offline-pill-row still wraps the "Take Survey Offline" button, which
           IS an in-flow element. */
        .offline-pill-row { text-align: center; }

        /* THE OFFLINE ROUTE, PINNED.
           Two things were wrong with this button in the reported screenshot:

           1. IT COLLIDED WITH THE CHIPS. It sat in the normal flow with a
              hand-tuned `margin-top: 3.5rem`, a number chosen when the only
              thing above it was the one-line "Viewing Offline" chip. The
              chips are position:fixed, so they take no space in the flow and
              nothing keeps them apart — once the taller two-line slow-
              connection banner appeared above it, the banner printed straight
              over the button and clipped the one action the page was offering.

           2. IT SCROLLED AWAY. The chips stay pinned while the page moves, so
              a visitor reading the dashboard was left with a warning fixed to
              the top and no visible way to act on it.

           Both are the same mistake — half the group was fixed and half was
           not. So the button joins the fixed stack, and its exact top is
           measured from the chips actually on screen rather than guessed (see
           syncOfflineStackPosition() near the bottom of this file). A magic
           margin cannot track a chip whose height depends on how its text
           wrapped.

           Gold, not navy: navy on this navy page is the low-contrast smudge
           visible in the report. This is the same gold as the header's Login
           button and the connection dialog's primary action — the page's
           established "this is the thing to press" colour. */
        .offline-pill-row { text-align: center; }

        .offline-survey-btn {
            position: fixed;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translateX(-50%);
            /* Overwritten in px by syncOfflineStackPosition() whenever a chip
               is up; this is the no-chips fallback. */
            top: calc(var(--offline-pill-top, 0.75rem) + env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px));
            /* Directly under .offline-pill (1030) so a chip never hides behind
               it, and under the mobile drawer (1035) like the chips. */
            z-index: 1029;

            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 0.45rem;
            max-width: min(94vw, 33rem);
            padding: 0.6rem 1.15rem;
            border-radius: 12px;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffd84d, #ffcc00);
            color: #251d3a;
            font-weight: 800;
            font-size: 0.86rem;
            line-height: 1.2;
            text-decoration: none;
            white-space: nowrap;
            box-shadow: 0 8px 20px -6px rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.5), 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
            transition: filter 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease;
        }
        .offline-survey-btn:hover { color: #251d3a; filter: brightness(1.05); transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(-1px); }
        .offline-survey-btn:active { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0); }
        .offline-survey-btn.d-none { display: none; }

        @media (max-width: 480px) {
            .offline-survey-btn { font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.55rem 0.95rem; max-width: calc(100vw - 20px); }
        }

        :root {
            --navy-950: #251d3a;
            --navy-900: #251d3a;
            --navy-800: #2a2550;
            --navy-700: #2a2550;
            --gold-500: #ffcc00;
            --gold-400: #ffcc00;
            --gold-300: #ffcc00;
            --gold-deep: #8a5a00; /* dark amber — passes AA contrast on light backgrounds */

            /* ---- Base-8 spacing scale — every margin/padding/gap below resolves to one of these ---- */
            --sp-1: 0.5rem;   /* 8px */
            --sp-2: 1rem;     /* 16px */
            --sp-3: 1.5rem;   /* 24px */
            --sp-4: 2rem;     /* 32px */
            --sp-5: 2.5rem;   /* 40px */
            --sp-6: 3rem;     /* 48px */
            --sp-7: 3.5rem;   /* 56px */
            --sp-8: 4rem;     /* 64px */
            --sp-10: 5rem;    /* 80px */
            --sp-12: 6rem;    /* 96px */

            /* ---- Typography scale ---- */
            --fs-xs: 0.75rem;
            --fs-sm: 0.875rem;
            --fs-base: 1rem;
            --fs-lg: 1.125rem;
            --fs-xl: clamp(1.25rem, 1.1rem + 0.6vw, 1.5rem);
            --fs-2xl: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2rem);
            --fs-3xl: clamp(1.8rem, 1.3rem + 2vw, 2.6rem);
            --fs-hero: clamp(2.25rem, 1.4rem + 4vw, 4.5rem);
        }

        /* --- GENERAL LAYOUT --- */
        html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
        body, html {
            margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: #1e293b;
            font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 1.6;
            /* Any single element overflowing horizontally by even a few px (a
               fixed-width card, an un-shrunk image, a stray negative margin)
               silently widens the whole page's layout viewport on mobile —
               the browser then "zooms out" to fit it all, which is what read
               as "can still zoom out" and the wide blank margins showing past
               the real content in every mobile screenshot so far. Clipping it
               here is the standard fix and has zero effect on desktop, where
               nothing was overflowing to begin with. */
            overflow-x: hidden;
        }
        h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 { line-height: 1.2; }

        .bg-image {
            /* 100%/100% instead of 100vw/100vh: for a `position:fixed`
               element, percentages resolve against the actual visual
               viewport, while `vw`/`vh` are defined off the *layout*
               viewport — the two can diverge by a scrollbar's width, or
               (on some mobile engines) by whatever the page's widest piece
               of content made the layout viewport expand to, so 100vw can
               render wider than what's actually visible. That mismatch is
               one contributor to the "content looks shifted on some phones"
               symptom this page has had — see the overflow-x:hidden note
               below for the other, larger one. */
            position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;
            background:url('<%- landingContent.hero.imageUrl %>');
            /* The CSPC monument sits in the upper half of this photo — on a
               tall mobile viewport, centering it vertically cropped the
               monument almost entirely out of frame. Anchoring to the top
               keeps it in view. */
            background-size: cover; background-position: top center; z-index: -2;
        }

        .bg-overlay {
            position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(37, 29, 58,0.92) 0%, rgba(37, 29, 58,0.85) 100%); z-index: -1;
        }

        body.dark-mode .bg-overlay { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(4,8,18,0.95) 0%, rgba(37, 29, 58,0.92) 100%); }

        /* .page-content, the Hero, and Services/About/Structure all stay fully
           transparent — the ONE fixed .bg-image/.bg-overlay pair (rendered once,
           pinned to the viewport, z-index -2/-1) is the only thing painting the
           photo/gradient, all the way down the page. That's what makes it read
           as a single continuous backdrop instead of separately-painted copies
           of the same image lining up imperfectly at each section boundary. */
        .page-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

        /* "Hover to see details" reads as broken instruction on a touch device
           with no hover — .tap-only-text is desktop-hidden by default, swapped
           for .hover-only-text inside the existing mobile media query below. */
        .tap-only-text { display: none; }
        .mobile-only-text { display: none; }

        /* --- SITE NAV LINKS --- */
        /* 3rem = 48px ≈ half an inch between DASHBOARD / SERVICES / ABOUT / STRUCTURE.
           .nav-inner already wraps (flex-wrap: wrap), so on a narrow desktop
           window the nav row drops below the brand instead of overflowing the
           header. Only applies here — below 62rem .site-nav becomes the stacked
           hamburger menu, which sets its own gap. */
        .site-nav { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-6); margin: 0 var(--sp-3); }
        .site-nav a { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-sm); letter-spacing: 0.4px; text-transform: uppercase; position: relative; padding-bottom: 4px; transition: color 0.25s ease; }
        .site-nav a::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; width: 0; height: 2px; background: var(--gold-400); transition: width 0.25s ease; }
        .site-nav a:hover { color: #fff; }
        .site-nav a:hover::after { width: 100%; }
        /* Scrollspy — whichever section is in view gets its nav link lit up gold
           with a persistent underline, kept in sync by IntersectionObserver. */
        .site-nav a.active { color: var(--gold-400); }
        .site-nav a.active::after { width: 100%; }

        /* --- FIXED HEADER --- */
        .sticky-top-section {
            position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 1000;
            background: rgba(37, 29, 58, 0.85);
            backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(150%); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(150%);
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.25);
            box-shadow: 0 4px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
            padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-4);
            display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-2);
        }

        .nav-inner {
            width: 100%; max-width: 75rem;
            display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-4);
        }

        body.dark-mode .sticky-top-section { background: rgba(4, 8, 18, 0.92); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.15); }

        .nav-left { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-2); }
        .nav-left img { width: 48px; height: 48px; object-fit: contain; }
        .header-text-container { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; }
        .header-title { font-size: var(--fs-lg); font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin: 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); line-height: 1.3; }
        .header-subtitle { font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: var(--gold-400); font-weight: 600; margin: 0; letter-spacing: 1px; line-height: 1.4; }

        .nav-right { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end; gap: var(--sp-2); margin-left: auto; }

        /* Hamburger toggle for .site-nav — hidden on desktop (the nav is already
           visible inline there), only shown/wired up inside the mobile media
           query below, where .site-nav switches from "hidden entirely" to a
           tap-to-open vertical menu instead of just disappearing with no
           replacement. */
        .nav-hamburger { display: none; background: transparent; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.4); color: #fff; width: 44px; height: 44px; min-width: 44px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 1.15rem; align-items: center; justify-content: center; cursor: pointer; }
        .nav-hamburger:hover { border-color: var(--gold-400); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); }
        .period-select {
            padding: var(--sp-1) var(--sp-2); border-radius: 50px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.4);
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); color: white; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-sm);
            outline: none; cursor: pointer; transition: border-color 0.25s ease, background 0.25s ease;
        }
        .period-select:hover { border-color: var(--gold-400); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); }
        .period-select option { background: var(--navy-900); color: white; }

        .auth-buttons { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); }
        .auth-buttons .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-1); border-radius: 50px; font-weight: 700; padding: var(--sp-1) var(--sp-3); font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: 1; }
        .auth-buttons .btn i { font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 1; }
        .btn-admin { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold-500), var(--gold-400)); color: var(--navy-950); border: none; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.45); position: relative; will-change: transform; transition: filter 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease; }
        .btn-admin:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); color: var(--navy-950); box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.55); }

        /* --- SPACER for fixed header --- */
        #header-spacer { width: 100%; }

        /* --- SECTION HEADING HELPER --- */
        .section-eyebrow { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-1); font-size: var(--fs-xs); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-500); margin-bottom: var(--sp-1); line-height: 1.4; }
        .section-eyebrow::before { content: ''; width: 28px; height: 2px; background: var(--gold-500); display: inline-block; flex-shrink: 0; }
        .section-title { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: var(--fs-3xl); color: var(--navy-900); margin: 0 0 var(--sp-3); }
        body.dark-mode .section-title { color: #f8fafc; }

        /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
           PERFORMANCE UTILITIES
           Every animated interaction below moves ONLY transform/opacity.
           Glow/lift effects use a pseudo-element whose OPACITY fades in —
           the box-shadow value itself is static, so nothing repaints the
           shadow geometry on hover.
        --------------------------------------------------------------- */
        .magnetic { display: inline-flex; will-change: transform; }

        .glow-card { position: relative; isolation: isolate; will-change: transform; }
        .glow-card::after {
            content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: inherit; padding: 1px;
            background: radial-gradient(280px circle at var(--mx, 50%) var(--my, 50%), rgba(255,199,44,0.65), transparent 45%);
            -webkit-mask: linear-gradient(#fff 0 0) content-box, linear-gradient(#fff 0 0);
            -webkit-mask-composite: xor; mask-composite: exclude;
            opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.35s ease; pointer-events: none; z-index: 2; will-change: opacity;
        }
        .glow-card:hover::after { opacity: 1; }
        .glow-card:hover { transform: translateY(-6px); }

        .pop-glow { position: relative; will-change: transform; }
        .pop-glow::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; inset: -6px; border-radius: inherit;
            box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(255, 204, 0,0.45);
            opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.3s ease; pointer-events: none; z-index: -1; will-change: opacity;
        }
        .pop-glow:hover::before { opacity: 1; }

        /* =========================================================
           HERO SECTION — the Transparency Dashboard (#dashboard) is now
           the FIRST thing inside this section, so it's the first thing
           visible on load. The welcome blurb (.hero-content) follows
           below it. This section paints NO background of its own: the
           fixed .bg-image / .bg-overlay layers (position:fixed, behind
           .page-content) are what show through here, so the hero photo
           + gradient doubles as the dashboard's backdrop with zero
           duplicate paint.
        ========================================================= */
        .hero-section {
            display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start;
            position: relative; text-align: center; padding: var(--sp-6) var(--sp-4) var(--sp-5);
        }

        @keyframes heroFadeUp {
            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }
            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
        }

        /* Scroll cue sits directly under the dashboard cards — just a small nudge
           of breathing room, no big empty gap before it. */
        .hero-scroll-cue {
            background: transparent; border: none; box-shadow: none;
            margin: 24px 0 0; width: max-content;
            color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55); font-size: var(--fs-xs); letter-spacing: 2.5px; text-transform: uppercase;
            display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-1); font-weight: 700;
            opacity: 0; animation: heroFadeUp 0.6s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: 0.2s;
        }

        @keyframes heroCueBounce {
            0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); opacity: 0.6; }
            50% { transform: translateY(8px); opacity: 1; }
        }
        .hero-scroll-cue-icon { display: inline-block; animation: heroCueBounce 2s ease-in-out infinite; }

        @media (max-width: 36rem) {
            .hero-section { padding: var(--sp-4) var(--sp-2) var(--sp-4); }
            .hero-scroll-cue { margin: var(--sp-3) 0 0; }
        }
        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            .hero-scroll-cue { animation: none; opacity: 1; }
            .hero-scroll-cue-icon { animation: none; }
        }

        /* =========================================================
           ABOUT SECTION
        ========================================================= */
        .about-section { padding: var(--sp-10) var(--sp-4); scroll-margin-top: 6.5rem; }
        .about-grid { max-width: 75rem; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 21.25rem 1fr; gap: var(--sp-7); align-items: center; }

        .profile-card {
            background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--navy-900), var(--navy-700));
            border-radius: var(--sp-3); padding: var(--sp-4) var(--sp-3) var(--sp-3); text-align: center;
            box-shadow: 0 20px 45px rgba(37, 29, 58,0.35); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 204, 0,0.25);
            position: relative; overflow: hidden;
        }
        .profile-card::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; top: -40%; right: -30%; width: 220px; height: 220px;
            background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255, 204, 0,0.25), transparent 70%); border-radius: 50%;
        }

        .profile-avatar {
            width: 140px; height: 140px; margin: 0 auto var(--sp-2); border-radius: 50%;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold-400), var(--gold-500));
            display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden;
            font-size: 3.5rem; color: var(--navy-950); border: 4px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.85);
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.3); position: relative; z-index: 1;
        }
        .profile-avatar img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top; }
        .profile-name { color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: var(--fs-lg); margin: 0; letter-spacing: 0.4px; position: relative; z-index: 1; line-height: 1.3; }
        .profile-role { color: var(--gold-300); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-sm); margin: var(--sp-1) 0 var(--sp-2); position: relative; z-index: 1; line-height: 1.4; }
        .profile-divider { width: 60px; height: 2px; background: rgba(255, 204, 0,0.5); margin: 0 auto var(--sp-2); position: relative; z-index: 1; }
        .profile-contact { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); position: relative; z-index: 1; }
        .profile-contact span { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-1); }
        .profile-contact a { color: var(--gold-300); text-decoration: none; }
        .profile-contact a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
        .profile-contact i { width: 16px; color: var(--gold-400); text-align: center; }

        /* About now sits on the always-dark hero photo (not a toggleable flat
           page background), so its text/badges use one light-on-dark look
           regardless of the site's light/dark mode. */
        .about-section .section-eyebrow { color: var(--gold-400); }
        .about-section .section-eyebrow::before { background: var(--gold-400); }
        .about-section .section-title { color: #fff; text-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); }
        .about-text { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); }
        .about-text p { font-size: var(--fs-lg); line-height: 1.75; font-weight: 400; margin: 0; }
        .about-badges { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-2); margin-top: var(--sp-3); }
        .about-badge {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-1); padding: var(--sp-1) var(--sp-2); border-radius: 50px;
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18); color: var(--gold-300);
            backdrop-filter: blur(8px); font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--fs-sm); will-change: transform;
        }
        .about-badge i { color: var(--gold-400); }
        .about-badge:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); }

        @media (max-width: 54rem) {
            .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; text-align: center; }
            .profile-card { max-width: 21.25rem; margin: 0 auto; }
            .about-badges { justify-content: center; }
        }

        /* =========================================================
           ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE SECTION
        ========================================================= */
        .org-section { padding: var(--sp-6) var(--sp-4) var(--sp-10); scroll-margin-top: 6.5rem; text-align: center; }
        .org-wrap { max-width: 75rem; margin: 0 auto; }
        .org-section .section-eyebrow { color: var(--gold-400); }
        .org-section .section-eyebrow::before { background: var(--gold-400); }
        .org-section .section-title { color: #fff; text-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); }

        .org-image-wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
        /* Kept as a solid white frame on purpose — the chart image itself is a
           light infographic, so a white card still gives the best contrast even
           though the section behind it is now the always-dark hero photo. */
        .org-image-frame {
            position: relative; border-radius: var(--sp-4); padding: var(--sp-2);
            background: linear-gradient(160deg, #ffffff 0%, #f4f6fb 100%);
            border: 1px solid rgba(37, 29, 58,0.08);
            box-shadow: 0 25px 60px -15px rgba(0,0,0,0.5), 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 204, 0,0.1);
            overflow: hidden; transition: transform 0.35s ease, box-shadow 0.35s ease;
        }
        .org-image-frame::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 4px;
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gold-400), var(--gold-500), var(--gold-400));
        }
        .org-image-frame:hover { transform: translateY(-6px); box-shadow: 0 30px 70px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.6), 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 204, 0,0.18); }
        .org-image {
            width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border-radius: var(--sp-3);
            box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(37, 29, 58,0.1);
        }

        @media (max-width: 36rem) {
            .org-image-frame { padding: var(--sp-1); border-radius: var(--sp-3); }
            .org-image { border-radius: var(--sp-2); }
        }

        /* =========================================================
           OUR SERVICES SECTION — flat accordion, one row per unit
           Cluster > Office > Services. Clusters are plain horizontal tabs
           (no framework, no extra JS libs); offices inside the active
           cluster render as a flat accordion. Expand/collapse animates a
           single grid-template-rows value — cheap even with ~40 offices.
        ========================================================= */
        /* No local background at all — stays transparent so the single fixed
           .bg-image/.bg-overlay (see top of file) shows through here too,
           continuing seamlessly from the Dashboard above with zero seam. */
        .services-section {
            padding: var(--sp-10) var(--sp-4); scroll-margin-top: 6rem; position: relative;
        }
        .services-header { text-align: center; max-width: 47.5rem; margin: 0 auto var(--sp-6); }
        .services-header .section-eyebrow { color: var(--gold-400); justify-content: center; }
        .services-header .section-eyebrow::before { background: var(--gold-400); }
        .services-header .section-title { color: #fff; text-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); }
        .services-header p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72); font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

        .services-wrap { max-width: 50rem; margin: 0 auto; }

        /* --- Cluster tabs (level 1) --- */
        .cluster-tabs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: stretch; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-3); margin: 0 0 var(--sp-5); }
        .cluster-tab-btn {
            flex: 1 1 11rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: var(--sp-2);
            padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); border-radius: 50px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
            backdrop-filter: blur(12px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); font-weight: 700;
            font-size: var(--fs-sm); font-family: inherit; cursor: pointer; text-align: center;
            transition: background 0.25s ease, color 0.25s ease, border-color 0.25s ease, transform 0.25s ease;
        }
        .cluster-tab-btn i { color: var(--gold-400); flex-shrink: 0; }
        .cluster-tab-btn:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.14); color: #fff; transform: translateY(-2px); }
        .cluster-tab-btn.active {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 204, 0,0.3), rgba(255, 204, 0,0.1));
            border-color: rgba(255, 204, 0,0.55); color: #fff;
        }

        /* --- Offices within the active cluster (level 2, accordion) --- */
        .services-accordion { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-3); }

        .accordion-item {
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); backdrop-filter: blur(12px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.14); border-radius: var(--sp-2); transition: border-color 0.3s ease, background 0.3s ease;
        }
        .accordion-item.open { border-color: rgba(255, 204, 0,0.35); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.11); }

        .accordion-header {
            width: 100%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--sp-2);
            padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); background: transparent; border: none; border-radius: var(--sp-2);
            color: #fff; text-align: left; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; transition: background 0.25s ease;
        }
        .accordion-header:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }

        .accordion-header-left { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-2); min-width: 0; }
        .accordion-icon {
            width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: var(--sp-1); background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold-400), var(--gold-500));
            display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--navy-950); font-size: var(--fs-sm); flex-shrink: 0;
        }
        .accordion-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; min-width: 0; }
        .accordion-name { font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: #fff; line-height: 1.4; }
        .accordion-count { font-size: var(--fs-xs); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; }

        .accordion-chevron { color: var(--gold-400); flex-shrink: 0; transition: transform 0.3s ease; will-change: transform; }
        .accordion-item.open .accordion-chevron { transform: rotate(180deg); }

        .accordion-panel { display: grid; grid-template-rows: 0fr; transition: grid-template-rows 0.3s ease; }
        .accordion-item.open .accordion-panel { grid-template-rows: 1fr; }
        .accordion-panel-inner { overflow: hidden; }

        .accordion-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0 var(--sp-3) var(--sp-3); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2); }
        .accordion-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-1); font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.68); line-height: 1.6; }
        .accordion-list i { color: var(--gold-400); font-size: 0.55rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; flex-shrink: 0; }

        @media (max-width: 36rem) {
            .services-section { padding: var(--sp-6) var(--sp-2); }
        }

        /* =========================================================
           DASHBOARD SECTION — transform-driven marquee (no scrollLeft)
        ========================================================= */
        .dashboard-section {
            width: 100%; padding: 0; scroll-margin-top: 6rem; position: relative; overflow: visible;
        }
        .dashboard-section::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; top: -15%; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
            /* Purely decorative glow, centered under the section via
               left:50%/translateX(-50%) — symmetric by construction, so it
               was never the cause of any LEFT/RIGHT imbalance. But at a
               fixed 70rem/40rem (1120px/640px) it's 3x wider than a phone
               screen, and .dashboard-section explicitly opts out of
               clipping it (overflow:visible, so the glow isn't cut off
               mid-fade at the section edge on desktop). With nothing
               between it and <body> that clips horizontally, that left it
               depending entirely on the page-wide `overflow-x: hidden`
               band-aid below to stay off the horizontal scroll axis — capped
               here instead so it never exceeds the viewport regardless of
               that global rule. */
            width: min(70rem, 100vw); height: min(40rem, 56vw); pointer-events: none; z-index: 0;
            background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(255, 204, 0,0.1) 0%, transparent 70%);
        }

        .dashboard-live-badge {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 5px 14px;
            border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.14); border: 1px solid rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.4);
            color: #4ADE80; font-size: var(--fs-xs); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.6px;
            width: fit-content; backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
        }
        .dashboard-live-dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: #22c55e; box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(34,197,94,0.6); animation: livePulse 1.8s infinite; }
        @keyframes livePulse {
            0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(34,197,94,0.55); }
            70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 7px rgba(34,197,94,0); }
            100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(34,197,94,0); }
        }

        .dashboard-toolbar { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; max-width: 75rem; margin: 0 auto var(--sp-3); padding: 0 var(--sp-4); position: relative; z-index: 1; }
        .period-dropbar {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; position: relative;
            padding: 10px 40px 10px 16px; border-radius: 999px;
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            transition: border-color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
        }
        .period-dropbar:hover { border-color: var(--gold-400); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.14); }
        .period-dropbar-icon { color: var(--gold-400); font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0; }
        .period-dropbar-caret { position: absolute; right: 16px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); font-size: 0.7rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); pointer-events: none; }
        .period-dropbar-select {
            appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none; border: none; background: transparent; outline: none;
            font-size: var(--fs-sm); font-weight: 700; color: #fff; cursor: pointer; padding-right: 4px;
        }
        .period-dropbar-select option { background: var(--navy-900); color: #fff; }

        .dashboard-header-block { text-align: center; max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto var(--sp-4); padding: 0 var(--sp-4); position: relative; z-index: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
        .dashboard-header-block .section-eyebrow { color: var(--gold-400); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
        .dashboard-header-block .section-eyebrow::before { background: var(--gold-400); }
        .dashboard-header-block .section-title {
            color: #fff; text-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
            font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 1rem + 1.4vw, 1.9rem); margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
        }
        .dashboard-header-block p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72); font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; max-width: 34rem; }
        .dashboard-offline-note {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;
            background: rgba(245,158,11,0.16); color: #fbbf24;
            border: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.35);
            padding: 0.35rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 50px;
            font-size: var(--fs-xs) !important; font-weight: 700;
            max-width: none !important;
        }

        /* KPI summary strip — glass tiles floating on the hero backdrop.
           Root cause of the "off-center on some phones only" bug: bare `1fr`
           grid tracks don't clamp to the space actually available — a grid
           item's default min-width is `auto` (its content's own min-content
           size, not 0), so if a tile's icon+text needs more room than an
           `1fr` track has, ALL tracks in that row grow to fit it instead of
           wrapping/shrinking, silently widening .kpi-strip (and therefore
           <body>) past the viewport. That only shows up once a phone is
           narrow enough for a tile's intrinsic content to exceed its track
           width — e.g. it reproduced at 320px but not 360px+ in testing —
           which is exactly the "some phones, not others" pattern reported.
           minmax(0, 1fr) caps each track at the space really available;
           min-width:0 on the tile itself (a flex container) does the same
           for its own icon+text row. */
        .kpi-strip {
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--sp-4);
            max-width: 87.5rem; margin: 0 auto var(--sp-5); padding: 0 var(--sp-4); position: relative; z-index: 1;
        }
        .kpi-tile {
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: var(--sp-2);
            padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
            backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(150%); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(150%);
            display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); min-width: 0;
            border-top: 3px solid var(--kpi-accent, var(--gold-400));
            transition: transform 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease, background 0.25s ease;
        }
        .kpi-tile:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); box-shadow: 0 16px 38px rgba(0,0,0,0.3); }
        .kpi-icon {
            width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: var(--sp-1); flex-shrink: 0;
            display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 1rem;
            background: var(--kpi-accent-soft, rgba(255, 204, 0,0.12)); color: var(--kpi-accent, var(--gold-500));
        }
        /* min-width:0 lets this text column actually shrink/wrap inside the
           flex row above instead of forcing .kpi-tile (and its grid track)
           wider — a flex child's default min-width is also `auto`. */
        .kpi-tile > div:last-child { min-width: 0; }
        .kpi-value { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 800; color: #fff; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
        .kpi-label { font-size: var(--fs-xs); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); margin-top: 2px; }
        @media (max-width: 62rem) { .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
        @media (max-width: 36rem) {
            /* Stayed 2-column here too instead of collapsing to a single
               stacked column — 2x2 fits comfortably even on narrow phones
               once the tile itself is sized down a bit. */
            .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.6rem; padding: 0 var(--sp-2); }
            .kpi-tile { padding: 0.7rem 0.7rem; gap: 0.5rem; }
            .kpi-icon { width: 30px; height: 30px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
            /* Was 1.05rem (16.8px) — a previous pass had shrunk this well
               past legibility for a "big number" stat; brought up to the
               22-24px target range so it still reads as the headline figure
               on the card. Label brought down + line-height tightened so
               the 2-3 word wrapped label doesn't add loose vertical space. */
            .kpi-value { font-size: 1.45rem; }
            .kpi-label { font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.25; margin-top: 2px; }
            .dashboard-live-badge { display: none; }

            /* Cluster pills: each has a flex-basis of 11rem (176px), so on a
               375-414px phone only one fit per row before wrapping — forced
               into a real 2-column grid instead, sized down to fit. */
            .cluster-tabs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.6rem; }
            .cluster-tab-btn { flex: none; padding: 0.65rem 0.5rem; font-size: 0.82rem; border-radius: var(--sp-2); gap: 0.4rem; }
            .cluster-tab-btn i { font-size: 0.95rem; }
        }

        /* No boxed "tray" anymore — just a plain flex viewport so the marquee
           still has something to clip against (overflow:hidden) for the
           auto-scroll/drag logic. Zero background/border/shadow of its own:
           the hero .bg-image/.bg-overlay show straight through. */
        .dashboard-container {
            display: flex; align-items: center; width: 100%; position: relative; overflow: hidden; z-index: 1;
            margin: 0 auto; max-width: 100rem;
        }

        .charts-track {
            display: flex; gap: var(--sp-5); padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-4); align-items: stretch;
            will-change: transform; touch-action: pan-y;
        }

        /* Charts are wide glass panels floating on the hero backdrop — a soft
           translucent fill + visible border + shadow so each graph reads as
           its own clearly-bounded card, while staying light enough that the
           photo/gradient behind it still comes through. */
        .chart-card {
            background: rgba(10,20,40,0.28);
            backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(150%); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(150%);
            display: flex; flex-direction: column;
            height: 63vh; min-width: min(88vw, 60rem); flex-shrink: 0;
            opacity: 0; transform: translateY(60px);
            transition: opacity 0.6s ease-out, transform 0.6s ease-out, box-shadow 0.25s ease, border-color 0.25s ease;
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.22); border-top: 3px solid var(--card-accent, var(--gold-400));
            border-radius: var(--sp-3); overflow: hidden;
            /* Kept deliberately shallow — .dashboard-container clips overflow (needed
               for the horizontal marquee), so a big diffuse shadow here would get a
               hard, visible cutoff at the container's bottom edge instead of fading
               into the hero backdrop. A tight shadow stays inside the clip region. */
            box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.25), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
            will-change: transform, opacity;
        }
        .chart-card.visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
        .chart-card:hover { transform: translateY(-6px); border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.35); box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }

        .card-header-custom { padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4) var(--sp-2); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.14); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; gap: var(--sp-2); }

        .chart-title-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
        .chart-icon-badge {
            width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 10px; flex-shrink: 0;
            display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.9rem;
            background: var(--card-accent-soft, rgba(255, 204, 0,0.12)); color: var(--card-accent, var(--gold-500));
        }
        .chart-title { font-size: var(--fs-lg); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px; color: #fff; margin: 0; line-height: 1.3; text-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.4); }

        .btn-back-custom { font-size: var(--fs-sm); font-weight: 600; padding: var(--sp-1) var(--sp-2); border-radius: var(--sp-1); }
        .chart-header-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); flex-shrink: 0; }
        .office-cluster-select {
            font-size: var(--fs-xs); font-weight: 600; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: var(--sp-1);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); color: #fff; cursor: pointer; max-width: 9rem;
            backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
        }
        .office-cluster-select:hover { border-color: var(--gold-400); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.14); }
        .office-cluster-select option { background: var(--navy-900); color: #fff; }
        /* min-height:0 overrides the flexbox default (min-height:auto) on this
           flex-grow child — without it, a flex item won't shrink below its
           content's intrinsic size, so the canvas (which Chart.js sizes via
           responsive:true/maintainAspectRatio:false against ITS parent) and
           this container end up in a feedback loop that overflows the fixed-
           height .chart-card, getting clipped by its overflow:hidden. This is
           what was cutting off pie slices / bar-chart axis labels at the card
           edge. */
        .canvas-container {
            position: relative; flex-grow: 1; min-height: 0; min-width: 0;
            padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4) var(--sp-4); display: flex; justify-content: stretch; align-items: stretch;
        }
        .canvas-container canvas { max-width: 100%; max-height: 100%; transition: opacity 0.35s ease, transform 0.35s ease; }
        .canvas-container.chart-transitioning canvas { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.96) translateY(8px); }
        .hint-text { font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55); margin-top: var(--sp-1); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.5; }

        /* =========================================================
           FOOTER
        ========================================================= */
        .site-footer {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy-900) 0%, var(--navy-950) 100%);
            color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); position: relative; overflow: hidden;
        }
        .site-footer::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
            background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--gold-400), transparent);
        }
        .footer-main { max-width: 75rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--sp-8) var(--sp-4) var(--sp-5); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1.2fr 1fr; gap: var(--sp-6); }

        .footer-brand-logo { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-2); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
        .footer-brand-logo img { width: 42px; height: 42px; object-fit: contain; }
        .footer-brand-title { color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: var(--fs-base); margin: 0; line-height: 1.35; }
        .footer-brand-title span { display: block; color: var(--gold-400); font-size: var(--fs-xs); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-top: 2px; }
        .footer-desc { font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55); margin: 0; }

        .footer-heading { color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: var(--fs-sm); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); position: relative; padding-bottom: var(--sp-1); line-height: 1.4; }
        .footer-heading::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; width: 32px; height: 2px; background: var(--gold-400); }

        .footer-links { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-2); }
        .footer-links a { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.62); text-decoration: none; font-size: var(--fs-sm); font-weight: 500; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-1); will-change: transform; transition: color 0.25s ease, transform 0.25s ease; }
        .footer-links a i { font-size: var(--fs-xs); color: var(--gold-400); will-change: transform; }
        .footer-links a:hover { color: var(--gold-300); transform: translateX(4px); }

        .footer-contact { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2); }
        .footer-contact li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-2); font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.62); line-height: 1.5; }
        .footer-contact i { color: var(--gold-400); font-size: var(--fs-base); width: 16px; margin-top: 2px; flex-shrink: 0; text-align: center; }
        .footer-contact a { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.62); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.25s ease; }
        .footer-contact a:hover { color: var(--gold-300); }

        .footer-socials { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--sp-2); margin-top: var(--sp-1); }
        .footer-socials a {
            width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); color: #fff; font-size: var(--fs-base);
            will-change: transform; transition: background 0.25s ease, border-color 0.25s ease, transform 0.25s ease;
        }
        .footer-socials a:hover {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold-500), var(--gold-400)); color: var(--navy-950);
            border-color: transparent; transform: translateY(-3px);
        }

        .footer-bottom {
            border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4); text-align: center;
            font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .footer-bottom strong { color: var(--gold-400); }

        @media (max-width: 62rem) {
            .footer-main { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--sp-5) var(--sp-4); }
        }
        @media (max-width: 36rem) {
            .footer-main { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-3) var(--sp-2); gap: var(--sp-4); text-align: center; }
            .footer-heading { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.82rem; }
            .footer-heading::after { left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); }
            .footer-brand-logo { justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
            .footer-brand-logo img { width: 34px; height: 34px; }
            .footer-desc { line-height: 1.5; font-size: 0.85rem; }
            /* Single centered column, not a 2-up grid — "Transparency
               Dashboard" wraps to two lines at this width, and a grid row
               pins its neighbor ("Our Services") to that same tall row
               height, leaving it stranded with a gap above it. A single
               column keeps every link's own height independent. */
            .footer-links { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; }
            .footer-links a { padding: 0.15rem 0; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; }
            .footer-links a i { margin-top: 0.25rem; }
            .footer-socials { justify-content: center; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
            .footer-contact { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.9rem 0.5rem; }
            .footer-contact li:first-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; text-align: left; }
            /* Email/phone/hours: icon stacked above centered, wrapped text
               instead of a horizontal row — a short cell (email) and a long
               one (phone number) sitting side-by-side in a row layout wrapped
               unevenly and looked lopsided; stacked-and-centered reads as
               deliberate regardless of each item's text length. */
            .footer-contact li { flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; gap: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }
            /* The extra 3rem right padding here used to keep the centered
               copyright line clear of the fixed theme-toggle FAB; that button
               is no longer included on this page, so it goes back to even
               side padding. */
            .footer-bottom { padding: var(--sp-2); font-size: 0.72rem; }
        }

        @media (max-width: 62rem) {
            .chart-card { min-width: 90vw; height: 55vh; }
            /* Single-row compact header: logo left, hamburger + login right.
               The 2-row stacked version (logo+title on row 1, hamburger+login
               on row 2) read as cluttered/misaligned — this is the standard
               mobile header pattern instead. The full org name/tagline is
               dropped here since the hero heading right below already
               introduces it prominently; showing it twice in a row was
               redundant and was what pushed the header tall in the first
               place. */
            .sticky-top-section { padding: 0.5rem var(--sp-2); }
            /* Hamburger far left, brand centered in the remaining space,
               Login far right — .nav-left gets flex:1 so it centers its own
               logo+text within whatever room is left between the other two,
               rather than sitting flush against the hamburger. */
            .nav-inner { gap: var(--sp-1); justify-content: space-between; }
            .nav-left { flex: 1; justify-content: center; }
            .nav-left img { width: 32px; height: 32px; }
            .nav-left { gap: 0.5rem; }
            /* Fixed short "CQA Portal" / "Login" labels instead of the full
               dynamic title/subtitle/login-label text (which was either too
               wide for one row, or truncated into an ugly "...") — swapped
               via a simple desktop/mobile text-toggle pair, same idea as the
               "Hover to see"/"Tap to drilldown" hint text above. */
            .desktop-only-text { display: none; }
            .mobile-only-text { display: inline; }
            .header-text-container { display: flex; }
            .header-title .mobile-only-text { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.3px; }
            .nav-right { flex-shrink: 0; gap: var(--sp-1); }
            .hover-only-text { display: none; }
            .tap-only-text { display: inline; }

            /* Nav links no longer just vanish on mobile — .nav-hamburger toggles
               .site-nav between hidden (default) and an open full-screen panel.
               Previously this pushed page content down (header grew taller, a
               spacer div resized to match) which looked fine right at the top
               of the page but read as "doesn't cover the page" once scrolled —
               the spacer/content reflow only accounted for the header's own
               box, not whatever was already scrolled past it. Making the open
               header stretch to the full viewport height (via .nav-open-header
               below, toggled in JS alongside .nav-open) sidesteps all of that:
               it's a real fixed-position overlay that covers the entire screen
               the same way regardless of scroll position, and never reflows
               the page underneath. */
            .nav-hamburger { display: inline-flex; }
            .site-nav { display: none; width: 100%; order: 3; }
            /* flex-basis MUST stay 100% here. The old rule used the shorthand
               `flex: 1`, which resolves to `flex-basis: 0` and silently beats
               the `width: 100%` above it — so instead of wrapping onto its own
               row the open menu stayed on the header row, squeezed into
               whatever space was left beside the brand/Login and clipping its
               own labels off the right edge. `flex: 1 1 100%` + min-width keeps
               it a genuine full-width row on every phone width. */
            .site-nav.nav-open {
                display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start;
                flex: 1 1 100%; width: 100%; min-width: 100%; max-width: 100%;
                margin: var(--sp-2) 0 0; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15);
                overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
            }
            .site-nav.nav-open a {
                padding: 1.1rem var(--sp-1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
                text-align: left; font-size: var(--fs-lg);
                /* Long labels wrap instead of running past the panel edge. */
                display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 0; white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
            }
            .site-nav.nav-open a::after { display: none; }

            /* Toggled on #siteHeader (alongside .nav-open on the nav itself) for
               as long as the mobile menu is open — expands the fixed header from
               its normal content-height box into a full-viewport panel so the
               whole page sits behind it, not just the header's own row. */
            .sticky-top-section.nav-open-header {
                /* Drops down over roughly the top half of the screen instead of
                   filling it. It used to stretch to 100dvh — that was chosen so
                   the panel would look identical whether or not the page was
                   already scrolled, but a whole blank screen for four links read
                   as a full-page takeover. It's position:fixed either way, so a
                   short panel still overlays the page (never reflows it) and
                   still behaves the same at any scroll position.
                   Height comes from the content, capped so a future longer menu
                   scrolls inside the panel rather than growing past half. */
                bottom: auto;
                height: auto;
                max-height: 55vh;
                max-height: 55dvh;
                background: rgba(37, 29, 58, 0.98);
                overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain;
                /* Notch / gesture-bar clearance on iPhone X-class and Android
                   gesture-nav devices. */
                padding-top: max(0.5rem, env(safe-area-inset-top));
                padding-bottom: max(var(--sp-2), env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
                padding-left: max(var(--sp-2), env(safe-area-inset-left));
                padding-right: max(var(--sp-2), env(safe-area-inset-right));
                /* Reads as a panel sitting above the page now that the page is
                   visible underneath it. */
                box-shadow: 0 18px 40px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
                border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 204, 0, 0.35);
            }
            body.dark-mode .sticky-top-section.nav-open-header { background: rgba(4, 8, 18, 0.98); }
            /* height:100% here was for the full-screen version; the panel is
               content-height now, so the row must not be stretched. */
            .sticky-top-section.nav-open-header .nav-inner { height: auto; align-content: flex-start; }
            /* The brand block is `flex: 1` on mobile; without min-width:0 its
               text sets the floor for how narrow it can get, which on 320px
               phones pushed the row wider than the screen. */
            .nav-inner > * { min-width: 0; }
            .nav-left { min-width: 0; }
            .header-text-container { min-width: 0; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 36rem) {
            .chart-card { min-width: 90vw; height: 38vh; }
            .about-section, .org-section { padding-left: var(--sp-2); padding-right: var(--sp-2); }
            /* Hamburger button was 44px (desktop/tablet base rule) on every
               screen it appears on — sized down to a denser 36px square to
               match the tightened header row on phones. */
            .nav-hamburger { width: 36px; height: 36px; min-width: 36px; font-size: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; }

            /* Hero profile card (Juvy Bustamante photo/name/title/contact) —
               the 140px avatar plus 32px/24px card padding was the single
               biggest "too big" element in the About section on a phone.
               Shrunk to an 84-96px range with proportionally tighter
               spacing between photo/name/divider/contact rows. */
            .profile-card { padding: 1.1rem 0.9rem 0.9rem; }
            .profile-avatar { width: 88px; height: 88px; font-size: 2.2rem; border-width: 3px; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
            .profile-role { margin: 0.4rem 0 0.6rem; }
            .profile-divider { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
            .profile-contact { gap: 0.5rem; }

            /* Section headings (Who We Are / Organizational Structure / Our
               Services all share .section-title) — was clamping to ~28.8px+
               min on phones; brought down to a flatter 26.4px so it reads as
               a marketing heading, not a desktop-scale hero headline. The
               Transparency Dashboard heading uses its own more specific
               .dashboard-header-block .section-title rule (already smaller)
               so it wins over this and is unaffected. */
            .section-title { font-size: 1.65rem; line-height: 1.18; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
            .about-text p { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; }
            .about-badges { gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
            .about-badge { padding: 0.45rem 0.85rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }

            /* Footer social icon circles: an earlier touch-target pass had
               bumped these to 44px; per this density pass they come back
               down to 36px (still a comfortably tappable circular icon,
               just not sized like a primary button). */
            .footer-socials a { width: 36px; height: 36px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
            .footer-main { gap: 1rem; }

            /* Office accordion rows (Our Services) — header padding/row gap
               were still desktop-scale (16px/24px vertical rhythm); tightened
               to the 8-12px density scale. .accordion-icon (36px) already
               matched the 36-40px target so it's left as-is. */
            .accordion-header { padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; }
            .accordion-name { font-size: 0.92rem; }
            .services-accordion { gap: 0.55rem; }
            .accordion-list { gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0 0.75rem 0.75rem; }

            /* Transparency Dashboard chart card header + hint text. */
            .card-header-custom { padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem 0.6rem; }
            .hint-text { font-size: 0.75rem; }
            /* .about-section, .org-section, .services-section all carry a
               desktop-scale 80px top/bottom padding (--sp-10) with no mobile
               override — tightened to --sp-4 (32px) here, the same amount of
               breathing room the header/hero already use on mobile. */
            .org-section { padding-top: var(--sp-4); padding-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
            .about-section, .services-section { padding-top: var(--sp-4); padding-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
            /* Chart card header (title + back button, or title + cluster-select +
               back button on the "By Office" card) was overflowing its fixed-width
               card on narrow phones since it never wrapped — let it wrap onto a
               second line instead of clipping/overlapping. */
            .card-header-custom { flex-wrap: wrap; row-gap: var(--sp-1); }
            .chart-header-actions { flex-wrap: wrap; row-gap: var(--sp-1); }
            .office-cluster-select { max-width: 100%; }
            .chart-title { font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
            .profile-contact a, .profile-contact span { word-break: break-word; }

            /* ---- Touch targets + readability pass ----
               Several controls were comfortably sized on desktop but landed
               under the ~44px tap-height guideline once scaled to phone
               widths: the Admin Login pill (~36px), the dashboard period
               dropdown (~40px), the per-chart cluster filter (~24px) and
               BACK button (~36px), and the footer's social icons (38px).
               Bumped padding/size on each — desktop's unprefixed rules are
               untouched. */
            .btn-admin { padding: 0.75rem var(--sp-3); }
            .period-dropbar { padding: 12px 40px 12px 16px; }
            .office-cluster-select { padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 0.8rem; }
            .btn-back-custom { padding: 0.6rem var(--sp-2); min-height: 40px; }
            /* .kpi-label and .footer-socials sizing consolidated into the
               density-pass rules earlier in this same media block (search
               "22-24px target range" / "36px (still a comfortably tappable"
               above) — this touch-target pass's older 0.8rem/44px values
               would otherwise win the cascade by appearing later here. */
            /* Footer link padding/gap consolidated into the earlier footer
               block above (search "line-height: 1.45" nearby) — keeping tap
               targets comfortable while fitting the whole footer into a much
               shorter mobile height overall. */
        }

        /* Respect reduced-motion preference: kill parallax/float, keep instant states */
        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            * { animation-duration: 0.001ms !important; animation-iteration-count: 1 !important; transition-duration: 0.001ms !important; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="bg-image"></div>
    <div class="bg-overlay"></div>

    <div class="sticky-top-section" id="siteHeader">
        <div class="nav-inner">
            <!-- Sits outside nav-left/nav-right on purpose: on mobile it's
                 CSS-ordered to the far left with nav-left centered between
                 it and nav-right (Login) — on desktop it's just plain
                 hidden (.nav-hamburger { display:none }), so its DOM
                 position here has zero effect on desktop layout. -->
            <button type="button" class="nav-hamburger" id="navHamburgerBtn" aria-label="Toggle navigation menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="siteNavList">
                <i class="fas fa-bars"></i>
            </button>

            <div class="nav-left">
                <img src="<%= landingContent.branding.logoUrl %>" alt="Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges Logo">
                <div class="header-text-container">
                    <h1 class="header-title"><span class="desktop-only-text"><%= landingContent.branding.title %></span><span class="mobile-only-text">CQA Portal</span></h1>
                    <p class="header-subtitle desktop-only-text"><%= landingContent.branding.subtitle %></p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <nav class="site-nav" id="siteNavList">
                <a href="#dashboard" data-nav-link>Dashboard</a>
                <a href="#services" data-nav-link>Services</a>
                <a href="#about" data-nav-link>About</a>
                <a href="#structure" data-nav-link>Structure</a>
            </nav>

            <div class="nav-right">
                <div class="auth-buttons">
                    <a href="/login" class="btn btn-admin magnetic"><i class="fas fa-sign-in-alt d-none d-sm-inline"></i><span class="desktop-only-text"><%= landingContent.branding.loginLabel %></span><span class="mobile-only-text">Login</span></a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="header-spacer"></div>

    <div class="offline-pill-row">
        <span id="offlineIndicator" class="offline-pill" role="status" title="No internet connection — showing the last data loaded while you were connected.">
            <span class="dot"></span><span class="label">Viewing Offline</span>
        </span>
        <!-- Visibility driven purely by navigator.onLine (see updateOfflineIndicator
             below) — never auto-navigated to; the user must click it themselves.
             Real account verification for whatever gets submitted through it only
             happens once back online, at POST /api/offline-surveys/verify-and-sync. -->
        <a href="/survey-offline" id="offlineSurveyBtn" class="offline-survey-btn d-none" title="Complete the survey now — your account is verified once you're back online">
            <i class="fas fa-clipboard-list"></i> Take Survey Offline
        </a>
        <!-- Same base .offline-pill class as #offlineIndicator (display:none
             until .is-visible is added) — deliberately the SAME visibility
             mechanism, not a mix of that and inline styles/Bootstrap's
             d-none, so there's exactly one way this element's visibility is
             ever controlled. -->
        <!-- .is-notice: this one carries a full sentence and a Retry button,
             unlike the two-word chip above. See /css/offline-pill.css for why
             that needs its own layout rather than the pill rule. -->
        <div id="serverUnavailableNotice" class="offline-pill is-notice" role="status">
            <i id="serverUnavailableNoticeIcon" class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i><span id="serverUnavailableNoticeText" class="label">Server temporarily unavailable. Please try again.</span>
            <button type="button" class="notice-retry-btn" onclick="checkServerHealth()">Retry</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page-content">

        <!-- ================= HERO SECTION ================= -->
        <section class="hero-section" id="hero">

            <!-- ================= TRANSPARENCY DASHBOARD — first thing visible on load ================= -->
            <section class="dashboard-section" id="dashboard">
                <div class="dashboard-header-block" data-reveal="fade-up">
                    <span class="section-eyebrow">Data &amp; Transparency</span>
                    <h2 class="section-title">Transparency Dashboard</h2>
                    <p>Live satisfaction survey results across clusters and offices. <span class="hover-only-text">Hover to see details, click to drill down.</span><span class="tap-only-text">Tap a chart to drill down.</span></p>
                    <p id="dashboardOfflineNote" class="dashboard-offline-note d-none"><i class="fas fa-wifi-slash me-1"></i>Viewing offline — showing the last data loaded while connected.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="dashboard-toolbar" data-reveal="fade-up" data-reveal-delay="100">
                    <div class="period-dropbar">
                        <i class="far fa-calendar-alt period-dropbar-icon"></i>
                        <select id="periodSelect" class="period-dropbar-select" onchange="changePeriod()">
                            <option value="p1">Jan - Jun 2026</option>
                            <option value="p2">Jul - Dec 2026</option>
                        </select>
                        <i class="fas fa-chevron-down period-dropbar-caret"></i>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="kpi-strip" id="kpiStrip">
                    <div class="kpi-tile" data-reveal="zoom-in" data-reveal-delay="0" style="--kpi-accent:#251d3a; --kpi-accent-soft:rgba(37, 29, 58,0.1);">
                        <div class="kpi-icon"><i class="fas fa-users"></i></div>
                        <div>
                            <div class="kpi-value" id="kpiRespondents">0</div>
                            <div class="kpi-label">Total Respondents</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-tile" data-reveal="zoom-in" data-reveal-delay="80" style="--kpi-accent:#22c55e; --kpi-accent-soft:rgba(34,197,94,0.12);">
                        <div class="kpi-icon"><i class="fas fa-face-smile"></i></div>
                        <div>
                            <div class="kpi-value" id="kpiSatisfaction">0%</div>
                            <div class="kpi-label">Overall Satisfaction</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-tile" data-reveal="zoom-in" data-reveal-delay="160" style="--kpi-accent:#ffcc00; --kpi-accent-soft:rgba(255, 204, 0,0.14);">
                        <div class="kpi-icon"><i class="fas fa-building"></i></div>
                        <div>
                            <div class="kpi-value" id="kpiOffices">0</div>
                            <div class="kpi-label">Offices Evaluated</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-tile" data-reveal="zoom-in" data-reveal-delay="240" style="--kpi-accent:#5B8DEF; --kpi-accent-soft:rgba(91,141,239,0.12);">
                        <div class="kpi-icon"><i class="fas fa-shield-halved"></i></div>
                        <div>
                            <div class="kpi-value" id="kpiAware">0%</div>
                            <div class="kpi-label">Citizen's Charter Awareness</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="dashboard-container">
                    <div class="charts-track" id="chartsTrack">

                        <div class="chart-card" id="card-c1" style="--card-accent:#22c55e; --card-accent-soft:rgba(34,197,94,0.12);">
                            <div class="card-header-custom">
                                <div class="chart-title-row">
                                    <div class="chart-icon-badge"><i class="fas fa-chart-pie"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <h3 id="c1-title" class="chart-title" data-main="Overall Ratings" data-drill="Total Overall Rating">Overall Ratings</h3>
                                        <div class="hint-text"><i class="fas fa-hand-pointer me-1"></i><span class="hover-only-text">Hover to see details • Click to drilldown</span><span class="tap-only-text">Tap to drilldown</span></div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <button id="c1-back" onclick="goBack('c1')" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary btn-back-custom d-none"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left me-1"></i> BACK</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="canvas-container"><canvas id="c1" style="cursor: pointer;"></canvas></div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="chart-card" id="card-c2" style="--card-accent:#5B7CD6; --card-accent-soft:rgba(90,124,214,0.12);">
                            <div class="card-header-custom">
                                <div class="chart-title-row">
                                    <div class="chart-icon-badge"><i class="fas fa-sitemap"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <h3 id="c2-title" class="chart-title" data-main="Satisfaction by Cluster" data-drill="Cluster Rating">Satisfaction by Cluster</h3>
                                        <div class="hint-text"><i class="fas fa-hand-pointer me-1"></i><span class="hover-only-text">Hover to see details • Click to drilldown</span><span class="tap-only-text">Tap to drilldown</span></div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <button id="c2-back" onclick="goBack('c2')" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary btn-back-custom d-none"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left me-1"></i> BACK</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="canvas-container"><canvas id="c2" style="cursor: pointer;"></canvas></div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="chart-card" id="card-c3" style="--card-accent:#ffcc00; --card-accent-soft:rgba(255, 204, 0,0.14);">
                            <div class="card-header-custom">
                                <div class="chart-title-row">
                                    <div class="chart-icon-badge"><i class="fas fa-building-columns"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <h3 id="c3-title" class="chart-title" data-main="Satisfaction By Office" data-drill="Office Rating">Satisfaction By Office</h3>
                                        <div class="hint-text"><i class="fas fa-hand-pointer me-1"></i><span class="hover-only-text">Hover to see details • Click to drilldown</span><span class="tap-only-text">Tap to drilldown</span></div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="chart-header-actions">
                                    <select class="office-cluster-select" onchange="setOfficeClusterFilter(this.value)">
                                        <option value="all">All Clusters</option>
                                    </select>
                                    <button id="c3-back" onclick="goBack('c3')" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary btn-back-custom d-none"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left me-1"></i> BACK</button>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="canvas-container"><canvas id="c3" style="cursor: pointer;"></canvas></div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="chart-card" id="card-c4" style="--card-accent:#5B8DEF; --card-accent-soft:rgba(91,141,239,0.12);">
                            <div class="card-header-custom">
                                <div class="chart-title-row">
                                    <div class="chart-icon-badge"><i class="fas fa-shield-halved"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <h3 id="c4-title" class="chart-title" data-main="CC Awareness" data-drill="CC Awareness Breakdown">CC Awareness</h3>
                                        <div class="hint-text"><i class="fas fa-hand-pointer me-1"></i>Click chart for details</div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <button id="c4-back" onclick="goBack('c4')" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary btn-back-custom d-none"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left me-1"></i> BACK</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="canvas-container"><canvas id="c4" style="cursor: pointer;"></canvas></div>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- "Services" already lives in the top nav, so no duplicate CTA here —
                 just the scroll cue, sitting directly under the dashboard cards. -->
            <div class="hero-scroll-cue">
                <span class="hero-scroll-cue-text">Scroll</span>
                <i class="fas fa-chevron-down hero-scroll-cue-icon"></i>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ================= OUR SERVICES SECTION ================= -->
        <section class="services-section" id="services">
            <div class="services-header" data-reveal="fade-up">
                <span class="section-eyebrow"><%= landingContent.services.eyebrow %></span>
                <h2 class="section-title"><%= landingContent.services.title %></h2>
                <p><%= landingContent.services.desc %></p>
            </div>

            <div class="services-wrap" data-reveal="fade-up">
                <div class="cluster-tabs" id="clusterTabs"></div>
                <div class="services-accordion" id="servicesAccordion"></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ================= ABOUT CQA SECTION ================= -->
